 arshin was equivalent to roughly 28 inches or 71 centimeters. It was a standard measure in trade and construction.\r\n\r\nSazhen: Another traditional Russian unit of length was the sazhen, mainly used in construction and land measurement. One sazhen was equal to about 2.134 meters or 7 feet.\r\n\r\nStandardization Efforts: Throughout this period, there were efforts to standardize measurement units for greater consistency and ease of trade and administration. This included the establishment of standards for traditional units like the verst and arshin.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2119, 'temperature': 0.2})
